WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.080
When you spend your life comparing&nbsp;
yourself to somebody else, it's hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.320
to build your own personality. That's&nbsp;
exactly what happened to Yelena Belova,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.720
Marvel's other Black Widow. Here's what you&nbsp;
need to know about this spy and assassin.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.760
In one of the more lurid origin stories in&nbsp;
Marvel history, back when the company was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.720
still publishing comics in its adults-only&nbsp;
MAX line, Yelena Belova's backstory was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:27.600
revealed in the series "Black Widow: Pale&nbsp;
Little Spider." Her trainer and mentor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.960
Colonel Starkovsky, is found killed in a Russian&nbsp;
fetish club. Starkovsky had been training her in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.600
combat since she was a pre-teen, and Yelena&nbsp;
thought of him as a father figure. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.480
he found himself thinking of her in a different&nbsp;
way, and felt tremendous guilt about it.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.640
He turned to the BDSM experts at club Fabrika,&nbsp;
headed by a mysterious woman named Nikki.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:55.520
She groomed a Yelena lookalike named Petra using&nbsp;
files Starkovsky had stolen. Petra would humiliate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:01.280
and degrade him while fulfilling his fantasies,&nbsp;
and this allowed Starkovsky to stay sane. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.640
Petra started to believe that she deserved to be&nbsp;
the Black Widow, and killed Starkovsky in a rage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.520
Yelena went undercover and encountered Nikki,&nbsp;
who eventually helped Yelena capture Petra.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.680
Yelena killed Petra without hesitation&nbsp;
and returned to receive her next orders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.760
as the new Black Widow. After she left,&nbsp;
it was revealed that Nikki was a spy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.840
and the whole mission was designed&nbsp;
to test Yelena' field readiness.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:24.480
"Whaaaat?"

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.840
"Why would you do that?"

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.160
Yelena Belova's first appearance came&nbsp;
in the Marvel Knights Inhumans series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:36.080
when General Yuri Stalyenko was leading an assault&nbsp;
on Attilan, the home of the Inhumans. The Inhumans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.480
had isolated themselves from the human race for&nbsp;
years for precisely this reason: they didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.960
want to engage with the wars and politics&nbsp;
of the human race. Of course, while Attilan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.160
was ruled by the wise Black Bolt, his brother&nbsp;
Maximus the Mad was always stirring up trouble.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.440
Maximus had secretly reached out to Stalyenko,&nbsp;
giving him information and technology that he knew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.560
would allow the invaders to pierce Attilan's&nbsp;
defenses and ultimately allow him to rule.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.000
In order to make this work, a lot of espionage&nbsp;
had to occur. Stalyenko sent his newly activated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.800
Black Widow, Yelena, to deliver what appeared&nbsp;
to be a gift to a U.S. ambassador. She told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.520
him that he needed to get it into the hands&nbsp;
of the Inhumans and it would act as a Trojan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:20.400
horse, emitting a frequency that would lower the&nbsp;
negative space barrier that protected Attilan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.160
The plan worked, as the ambassador gave&nbsp;
the gift to an Inhuman diplomat after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:28.480
the U.S. refused to intervene directly to&nbsp;
stop the attacks on Attilan. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.640
Black Bolt knew what Maximus had planned&nbsp;
all along and went along with it before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.280
he crushed Stalyenko's forces and made it&nbsp;
appear as though Attilan had been destroyed.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.520
During the 1999 Black Widow miniseries,&nbsp;
Colonel Khan of the Rhapastanian army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:48.880
commissioned a scientist named Dr. Didier&nbsp;
Ines to create a biological weapon called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.680
the Deathless Frenzy. This bio-toxin,&nbsp;
once it infected its targets, turned them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.960
into invincible berserker warriors until it&nbsp;
cycled through their bodies and ravaged them.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.960
Naturally, the U.S. and Russia didn't&nbsp;
want a rogue state in possession of such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.960
a dangerous weapon. More to the point,&nbsp;
both countries wanted it for themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.360
So both countries sent their Black Widows to&nbsp;
retrieve it: Natasha Romanoff for the U.S.,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.280
and Yelena Belova for Russia. In their&nbsp;
first encounter, Natasha's experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.680
overcame Yelena's surprise factor and&nbsp;
sheer ruthlessness. Yelena immediately told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:23.840
Natasha that she was the new Black Widow,&nbsp;
revealing her obsession with her. Natasha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.320
understood how to use that to her advantage&nbsp;
as she coolly manipulated the younger spy.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.600
Natasha kidnapped Ines and forced him to create&nbsp;
a vaccine — then she drew Yelena out of hiding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.880
and faked her own death, manipulating Yelena&nbsp;
to go back to Rhapastan. Natasha genuinely felt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.800
sorry for Yelena and the life that was chosen&nbsp;
for her, but that didn't mean that she wasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.600
going to use her. Natasha went undercover&nbsp;
to vaccinate Khan's men and destroyed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.320
virus while Yelena served as her distraction.&nbsp;
When Yelena tried to kill her, Natasha said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.720
that Yelena's passion for the game wouldn't&nbsp;
let her do it just yet... and she was right.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.000
Yelena's next encounter with Natasha in&nbsp;
the 2001 "Black Widow" miniseries was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.440
even more one-sided and brutal.&nbsp;
During their first encounter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.960
Natasha learned that the new head of the Red&nbsp;
Room was none other than General Yuri Stalyenko,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.760
a former mob-level thug who managed to worm&nbsp;
his way into a position of power. Natasha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:21.360
had SHIELD abduct Yelena from her apartment and&nbsp;
perform "Face/Off"-style facial cosmetic surgery.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.400
"It's like looking in a mirror, only...not."

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:29.360
A confused Yelena woke up in Natasha's New&nbsp;
York apartment with Natasha's face and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.480
cheery Daredevil there to hit on her. Natasha,&nbsp;
as Yelena, picked a fight with her in public,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.680
baiting Yelena, as Natasha, to shoot her.&nbsp;
A confused but angry Yelena obliged, even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.200
as Natasha was really pretending to be Yelena,&nbsp;
taunting her that she was too old and too slow.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.600
The whole point of this was for Natasha to&nbsp;
get in with Stalyenko and learn his plans. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:54.480
had a bunch of nukes stashed in New York, and&nbsp;
though Stalyenko suspected she wasn't really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.560
Yelena and sent an assassin after her, she&nbsp;
was still a step ahead of him. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.440
SHIELD was pretending to chase&nbsp;
Yelena all around New York,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.920
exhausting the confused spy before&nbsp;
Daredevil finally let her off the hook.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.040
Natasha then made sure Yelena heard Stalyenko&nbsp;
admit that Yelena was expendable and he'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.920
use her without hesitation. After the Widows&nbsp;
captured him, Yelena attacked Natasha. Natasha&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:20.640
revealed that she was trying to save Yelena and&nbsp;
teach her that everyone gets used in espionage.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.720
When Natasha met Yelena for the third time,&nbsp;
things got weird. Well, weirder. The Red Room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.760
was hunting down former Black Widow agents, but&nbsp;
Natasha turned the tables and killed her pursuers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:36.880
and their accomplice, the CEO of an American&nbsp;
drug company. That made her a wanted fugitive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.200
so she found her way to Cuba, where she knew&nbsp;
Yelena had defected. This is where their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:46.400
relationship thawed, as a mellow Yelena had been&nbsp;
living it up after making millions as a lingerie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.880
model and business owner. She had retired&nbsp;
from the spy game and was living in luxury.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:54.800
She also provided a place for girls to&nbsp;
get off the street and gave them medicine.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.520
She was happy to offer safe harbor for Natasha&nbsp;
in exchange for Natasha roughing up some drug&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.320
suppliers who had jacked up the prices on their&nbsp;
supply. Natasha did this, but realized that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.360
dealers were working for Gynacon, the company&nbsp;
whose CEO she had killed. Natasha was later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:13.760
kidnapped by a couple of killers looking for&nbsp;
revenge, but Yelena and Daredevil rescued her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:18.560
after she had been drugged. Natasha stayed in Cuba&nbsp;
for a while, recovering, and they became friends.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:25.040
The next time Yelena popped up in New Avengers&nbsp;
#6, she was back in the spy game and had started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.360
working for SHIELD, although she was part&nbsp;
of a renegade unit that was mining Savage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:34.880
Land Vibranium. Unlike Wakandan Vibranium,&nbsp;
which absorbed sound, Savage Land Vibranium&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:40.080
destroyed the integrity of anything metallic. The&nbsp;
New Avengers came across the operation while they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.360
were hunting down Karl Lykos, a man who could&nbsp;
transform into a sentient pteranodon called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:51.840
Sauron, an energy leech who specifically homed&nbsp;
in on mutant energy. Belova and her unit also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:56.400
attacked the New Avengers, but Sauron burned&nbsp;
her with fire before he was finally defeated.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.800
Belova was whisked away by AIM, who&nbsp;
saved her life and offered her a deal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:04.880
Her body was now permanently scarred&nbsp;
and broken, but if she agreed to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:08.640
her consciousness transferred into&nbsp;
the body of the new Super Adaptoid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:12.480
her power would be limitless and she could&nbsp;
get back at the New Avengers. The Super&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:17.760
Adaptoid could absorb the powers of anyone&nbsp;
upon contact, and those powers would stack.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.040
In "New Avengers Annual #1," Yelena attacked&nbsp;
Avengers Tower. When she absorbed the powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:26.960
of the Sentry, it appeared that there&nbsp;
was no way the Avengers could stop her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.440
Iron Man summoned his entire armory of suits&nbsp;
against her, wearing her down as they fought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:36.400
her remotely. That gave the Sentry time to&nbsp;
activate his other, evil self within him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:42.320
the Void, and push it in Yelena. Sensing a&nbsp;
mission failure, AIM destroyed Yelena remotely.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.160
Yelena Belova has often been involved in many&nbsp;
hidden corners and cracks of the Marvel Universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.040
One of the stranger ones was her membership&nbsp;
in a secret team called Vanguard, an elite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:58.320
black-ops squad that specialized in assassinations&nbsp;
across the world. Their leader was Trenton Craft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:03.520
alias Colonel America, the product of a companion&nbsp;
to the Super Soldier program of World War II.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.240
Whereas Captain America was developed as a peak&nbsp;
physical specimen, Craft was developed as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:13.680
most powerful telekinetic mind on the planet.&nbsp;
However, he was too powerful and couldn't control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:18.400
his powers, which led to a disastrous first&nbsp;
mission where he destroyed an entire city.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:23.120
He spent the next 60 years secretly&nbsp;
honing his powers as he oversaw this team.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:28.000
Craft was seemingly assassinated, but it turned&nbsp;
out to be a complicated series of double crosses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:32.560
that culminated with Craft showing up alive&nbsp;
and deciding to obliterate the team since they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:37.680
were compromised. Whether or not this version of&nbsp;
Yelena survived the end of the story is unclear.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.600
Yelena disappeared from the public eye until&nbsp;
Norman Osborn found her breaking into a SHIELD&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.480
facility, which led to an offer for her to lead&nbsp;
his team of Thunderbolts during Dark Reign.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:52.160
She proved to be a capable tactician&nbsp;
and leader of the group. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.760
this wasn't actually Yelena at all&nbsp;
— it was once again Natasha Romanoff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.360
assuming Yelena's identity in order to&nbsp;
infiltrate the Thunderbolts for Nick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.160
Fury. She secretly reported her activities&nbsp;
to Fury, who directed her on her missions.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.920
Of course, this wasn't actually&nbsp;
Fury. Osborn knew she wasn't Belova,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.920
because he had Belova in a stasis tube,&nbsp;
recovering from her destruction as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:16.880
Super Adaptoid. So he intercepted Natasha's&nbsp;
communications and pretended to be Fury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:21.520
hoping that Natasha would eventually lead&nbsp;
him to his foe. He had the Thunderbolts track&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.600
down Songbird and then ended the charade,&nbsp;
ordering the Thunderbolts to kill them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.880
Natasha and Songbird managed to escape when&nbsp;
several of the Thunderbolts turned on each other.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.600
Some time later, Andrew Forson,&nbsp;
the Scientist Supreme of AIM,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:40.160
recovered that stasis tube from Osborn&nbsp;
and revived Yelena. AIM had purchased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.400
the island of Barbuda and decided to&nbsp;
declare themselves a sovereign nation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:49.120
Barbuda became a haven for super-villains,&nbsp;
and Yelena became its Minister of State.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:53.280
The Secret Avengers stormed the facility&nbsp;
as things began to fall apart for AIM.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:58.080
A captured Mockingbird tried to escape&nbsp;
but was met by Yelena, and they fought.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.880
At the end of the fight, Mockingbird was shot&nbsp;
and killed... except it wasn't Mockingbird. She'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:08.240
placed a hologram device on Yelena that made her&nbsp;
look like Mockingbird. Yelena was dead, yet again.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.200
If you're wondering how Yelena found time&nbsp;
to have all these adventures when seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.360
every story involves her dying or captured&nbsp;
by S.H.I.E.L.D., there's a simple answer:

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:22.800
"You're clones. You're copies of&nbsp;
people out here in the world."

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.800
"Clones? What?"

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:30.320
The Red Room spy program that produced deadly&nbsp;
female spies quite literally produced deadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:35.520
female spies. They kept clones of Natasha and&nbsp;
Yelena on hand and had a psychic operative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:40.880
named Epsilon Red, who maintained all of their&nbsp;
memories and could download them into new bodies.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:46.080
Natasha Romanoff was killed by the HYDRA version&nbsp;
of Captain America during Secret Empire. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:50.400
the Red Room activated a new Natasha clone.&nbsp;
When the clone became aware of all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:56.640
she used a blank slate Yelena clone as fodder to&nbsp;
impersonate SHIELD agent Sally "Skids" Blevins in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:02.000
order to fake Sally's death. She then took apart&nbsp;
the Red Room and destroyed all of the clones.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:06.720
Natasha sent another Yelena clone disguised&nbsp;
as her in order to throw off Hawkeye and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:11.360
Winter Soldier... but not before she killed&nbsp;
the real Yelena. Then she killed the clones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:15.840
as well to put an end to her friend and&nbsp;
rival, once and for all… at least until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.440
the character likely gets a well-earned&nbsp;
reboot following the "Black Widow" film.

